# Grafana Cloud OTLP credentials (Add new connection → OpenTelemetry).
# Copy to .env — never commit the real file.
# Used by Alloy for all telemetry (ktranslate SNMP/flow/syslog + gnmic).
GC_OTLP_URL=https://otlp-gateway-prod-YOUR-REGION.grafana.net/otlp
GC_OTLP_ACCOUNT=000000
GC_OTLP_KEY=glc_REPLACE_ME

# Optional — fan-out the same telemetry to more Grafana Cloud stacks.
# When a suffix is fully set, Alloy adds that sink
# (make generate → alloy/otlp-export.generated.alloy). Leave unset for single-stack.
# GC_OTLP_URL_2=https://otlp-gateway-prod-OTHER-REGION.grafana.net/otlp
# GC_OTLP_ACCOUNT_2=000000
# GC_OTLP_KEY_2=glc_REPLACE_ME
# GC_OTLP_URL_3=https://otlp-gateway-prod-us-west-0.grafana.net/otlp
# GC_OTLP_ACCOUNT_3=000000
# GC_OTLP_KEY_3=glc_REPLACE_ME

# Grafana HTTP API — used by the one-click scripts (oneclick/) to import the
# network-lab dashboards with a token (no OAuth). Create the token at:
#   Grafana → Administration → Users and access → Service accounts → Add token (Editor/Admin)
# GRAFANA_URL=https://yourstack.grafana.net
# GRAFANA_TOKEN=glsa_REPLACE_ME
#
# KtransToGrafana checkout (dashboard JSON source of truth). Default: ../KtransToGrafana
# KTRANS_UPSTREAM=/path/to/KtransToGrafana
# Grafana Cloud Access Policy token with the `stack-plugins:write` scope — lets the
# one-click scripts install the panel plugins (andrewbmchugh-flow-panel,
# netsage-sankey-panel) via the grafana.com Cloud API. Create at:
#   Grafana Cloud portal → Access Policies → new policy (scope: stack-plugins:write) → Add token
# (Or add the stack-plugins:write scope to your OTLP access policy and reuse GC_OTLP_KEY.)
# GC_STACK_TOKEN=glc_REPLACE_ME
# Optional (Windows): gcx path + context for scripts/import-network-join-demo-gcx.py
# GCX_BIN=C:/path/to/gcx.exe
# GCX_CONTEXT=yourstack

# Identifies this ktranslate host. Alloy stamps it as deployment_host on every
# signal; it also suffixes service.name (e.g. ktranslate-snmp-srl-<host>).
# Leave blank to auto-resolve from hostname; `make generate` writes
# compose-host.generated.env so compose always picks it up (no per-machine .env edit).
KTRANS_HOST=

# Colocated EC2 + k3s collectors: discovery uses host network and OTLP → k3s Alloy.
# Colocated AWS demo: HQ hub + two branch offices (see topology-colocated.clab.yml).
# Laptop lab leaves this unset (default profile = laptop, 5-node fabric).
# Do not set snmp-min here — use `make alloy-snmp-min` (1× SRL + Alloy, no Clos).
# LAB_FABRIC_PROFILE=colocated
# COLLECTOR_RUNTIME=k3s
# KTRANSLATE_OTEL_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:4317

# Topology / entity graph label (Prometheus tester_id). Defaults to KTRANS_HOST
# or hostname when blank. Set explicitly for a stable id across machines.
LAB_TESTER_ID=network-lab

# Optional topology_exporter (SNMP device graph + BGP). Off by default to save RAM.
# When enabled: LAB_TOPOLOGY_EXPORTER=1 then `make topology-up` (compose profile topology).
# LLDP edges still come from gnmic without this collector.
# LAB_TOPOLOGY_EXPORTER=0

# Optional Alloy-native SNMP poll (parallel to ktranslate — does not replace it).
# Build the fork overlay first: make alloy-network-image
# Then set:
#   ALLOY_IMAGE=srl-local/alloy:network-dev
#   LAB_ALLOY_SNMP=1
# Scrape tiers (each optional). Default hot+cold. Minimum useful = hot only:
#   LAB_ALLOY_SNMP_TIERS=hot
#   LAB_ALLOY_SNMP_TIERS=hot,cold
#   LAB_ALLOY_SNMP_TIERS=hot,cold,topology
# Legacy: LAB_ALLOY_SNMP_TOPOLOGY=1 adds topology when TIERS is unset.
# Fleet Management (marcnetterfield1: https://fleet-management-prod-008.grafana.net):
#   LAB_ALLOY_FLEET=1
#   LAB_ALLOY_FLEET_SNMP=1        # stub local SNMP; upsert network.pipeline.alloy
#   LAB_ALLOY_FLEET_EVENTS=1      # stub local traps+syslog (Fleet already has them)
#   LAB_ALLOY_FLEET_NETFLOW=1     # stub local netflow (Fleet already has it)
#   LAB_ALLOY_FLEET_DISCOVERY=1   # discovery.snmp in Fleet (needs FROM_SOURCE image)
#   LAB_ALLOY_SNMPTRAP=1          # otelcol.receiver.snmptrap :1620; retarget SRL trap-group
#   LAB_ALLOY_SYSLOG=1            # loki.source.syslog :1514; retarget SRL remote-server
#   LAB_KTRANSLATE=0              # scale ktranslate Deployments to 0; Alloy owns SNMP/flow/traps/syslog
#   LAB_ALLOY_NETFLOW=1           # otelcol.receiver.netflow :2055 + sFlow :6344 (not ktranslate 9995/6343)
#   LAB_ALLOY_NETFLOW_METRICS=1   # default ON: signaltometrics → network.io.by_flow (use rate())
#   LAB_ALLOY_NETFLOW_LOGS=0      # optional: punt decoded records to OTLP logs (experimental)
#   ALLOY_NETWORK_FROM_SOURCE=1 make alloy-network-image
#   GC_FM_URL=https://fleet-management-prod-008.grafana.net
#   GC_FM_TOKEN=…                 # fleet-management:write to upsert
#   make alloy-fleet-up
# Fallback (overlay image + sidecar): LAB_ALLOY_FLEET_DISCOVERY=0
# Discovery (named snmp.yml auths + sysObjectID→module tiers) then scrape:
#   make alloy-snmp-discover && make alloy-snmp-up
# Hot≈60s alerting (if_mib + CPU/mem + chassis), cold≈5m metadata
# (ifAlias/sysDescr; set LAB_ALLOY_SNMP_COLD_INTERVAL=30m for fleet).
# BGP neighbor events are traps/syslog, not a scrape. Topology≈15m optional LLDP.
# Optional: LAB_ALLOY_SNMP_HOT_INTERVAL=60s
# Optional: LAB_ALLOY_SNMP_COLD_INTERVAL=5m
# Optional: LAB_ALLOY_SNMP_COLD_TIMEOUT=4m
# Optional: LAB_ALLOY_SNMP_TOPOLOGY_INTERVAL=15m
# Optional: SNMP_AUTHS=   (snmp_exporter auths: YAML overlay for Fleet
#   discovery.snmp / prometheus.exporter.snmp. Empty falls back to the image
#   library. Example: fork snmp/auths.example.yml. Do not put this in Fleet.)
# Optional: ALLOY_SNMP_AUTHS=public_v2   (try-order of named auths)
# Optional: ALLOY_SNMP_CIDRS=172.20.20.2/32,172.20.20.3/32
# Optional: ALLOY_SNMP_GROUP=hq          (force one discovery job; default is
#   hq on laptop, or hq+branch1+branch2 on LAB_FABRIC_PROFILE=colocated)
# Docs: docs/alloy-network-fork.md
# LAB_ALLOY_SNMP=0
# LAB_ALLOY_SNMP_TOPOLOGY=0
# LAB_ALLOY_FLEET=0
# LAB_ALLOY_FLEET_SNMP=0
# LAB_ALLOY_FLEET_DISCOVERY=1
# LAB_ALLOY_SNMPTRAP=0
# LAB_ALLOY_SYSLOG=0
# LAB_ALLOY_NETFLOW=0
# LAB_ALLOY_NETFLOW_METRICS=1
# LAB_ALLOY_NETFLOW_LOGS=0
# ALLOY_SRC=../alloy

# Optional — ktranslate snmp-profiles GitHub fork (profile_git_url, ktranslate#803).
# `make generate` stamps this into poller + discovery YAML. Recreate SNMP containers
# after changing it (clone happens at process start). Leave blank for the image library.
# PROFILE_GIT_URL=https://github.com/YOU/snmp-profiles
# PROFILE_GIT_COMMIT=                    # optional SHA; empty = HEAD of main
# A groups/<name>.env may set the same vars to override per credential group.
# Private fork / non-main branch (ktranslate#869 / #877) — compose passes these through:
# KT_GIT_ACCESS_USERNAME=
# KT_GIT_ACCESS_TOKEN=
# KT_GIT_PULL_BRANCH=

# Container image pins (leave blank for :latest)
# Dev build with OTLP CHF fix (flow_only): make ktranslate-dev-image → set line below
# KTRANSLATE_IMAGE=srl-local/ktranslate:otel-chf-dev
KTRANSLATE_IMAGE=
ALLOY_IMAGE=
GNMIC_IMAGE=
TOPOLOGY_EXPORTER_IMAGE=

# SNMP community for topology-exporter (matches groups/srl-hq.env)
SNMP_COMMUNITY=public

# Optional — Telegraf flex PoC SSH (make telegraf-poc); ContainerLab SR Linux defaults
# SRL_SSH_USER=admin
# SRL_SSH_PASSWORD=NokiaSrl1!

# Per-container OTEL_SERVICE_NAME is set in compose (ktranslate-flow, ktranslate-sflow, …).
# Do not set a global OTEL_SERVICE_NAME here — it would override flow/sflow naming.
OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_COMPRESSION=gzip
# softflowd on clients emits NetFlow v9
NF_SOURCE=netflow9
# flow_dns — ktranslate reverse DNS for src_host / dst_host on NetFlow rollups.
FLOW_DNS=flow_dns:53
FLOW_DNS_UPSTREAM=host.docker.internal
FLOW_DNS_EXTRA_HOSTS=client1:172.17.0.1,client2:172.17.0.2
FLOW_DNS_DOCKER_NETWORK=clab
FLOW_DNS_DOCKER_NODES=spine1 leaf1 leaf2 client1 client2
FLOW_DNS_IMAGE=
SYSLOG_SOURCE=0.0.0.0:1514

# Push-button telemetry after make up (softflowd, syslog, traps, traffic, events-loop)
# LAB_AUTO_TRAFFIC=0
# LAB_AUTO_INTERNET_PROBES=0
# LAB_AUTO_EVENTS=0
# LAB_AUTO_SYNTHETIC_TRAPS=1   # opt-in host snmptrap suite (default off; SRL sends real traps)
# INTERNET_PROBE_INTERVAL_SEC=120
# INTERNET_PROBE_HOSTS=grafana.com,github.com,www.kentik.com

# Per-container memory limits (scripts/compute-limits.sh on make up)
# Uses /proc/meminfo on Linux, docker info on Docker Desktop (Mac/Windows), or sysctl on macOS.
# MEM_LIMITS=off
# MEM_BUDGET_FRACTION=0.80
# MEM_SNMP_MAX=4g

# Optional — NetBox (OSS or Cloud). Used when DISCOVERY_SOURCE=netbox in groups/*.env
# and by make netbox-sync / Orb PoC work.
#
# Local OSS (preferred for laptop):
#   make netbox-oss-up    # writes the four vars below to this file
#   make netbox-sync
# NETBOX_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000
# NETBOX_HOST_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000
# NETBOX_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/dcim/devices/
# NETBOX_TOKEN=REPLACE_ME
# UI login (colocated / OSS) — generated by rotate-netbox-admin-password.py / netbox-colocated-bringup
# NETBOX_ADMIN_USER=admin
# NETBOX_ADMIN_PASSWORD=  # never commit; not admin/admin
# NETBOX_PUBLIC_URL=http://network-o11y-netbox-ui-….elb.us-east-1.amazonaws.com:8000
#
# Cloud trial:
# NETBOX_URL=https://YOUR-TENANT.cloud.netboxapp.com
# NETBOX_HOST_URL=https://YOUR-TENANT.cloud.netboxapp.com
# NETBOX_API_URL=https://YOUR-TENANT.cloud.netboxapp.com/api/dcim/devices/
# NETBOX_TOKEN=nbt_REPLACE_ME

# Optional — Orb agent sidecar (make orb-up). Default dry-run → local/orb/out/*.json
# Orb agent — prefer AWS colocated (make orb-colocated). Laptop: make orb-up-local (heavy).
# ORB_DRY_RUN=1
# ORB_SNMP_TARGETS=172.20.20.0/24
# ORB_SNMP_COMMUNITY=public
# ORB_PKTVISOR=0
# ORB_OTLP=0   # set 1 when Alloy is up (or auto-on with ORB_PKTVISOR=1)
# ORB_AGENT_IMAGE=netboxlabs/orb-agent:latest
# ORB_AGENT_NAME=network-o11y-colocated
# Live Diode (ORB_DRY_RUN=0):
# DIODE_CLIENT_ID=
# DIODE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# ORB_DIODE_TARGET=grpc://127.0.0.1:8080/diode

# ContainerLab management Docker network (clab 0.72+ uses the shared "clab" bridge)
CLAB_NETWORK=clab

# Staggered bring-up (default on): pause between fabric nodes and collectors.
# Reduces simultaneous SR Linux boot + compose pull load on resource-constrained laptops.
# LAB_STAGGER=0           parallel bring-up (make up-parallel)
# LAB_STAGGER_SECS=25     seconds between each component (default)
# LAB_STAGGER_FABRIC=0    skip fabric node stagger (collectors still stagger)
# LAB_STAGGER_COLLECTORS=0  compose up -d all collectors at once
# LAB_STABILIZE_WAIT_SECS=45  initial settle before sr_cli polls in make stabilize
# LAB_SR_CLI_TRIES=120        sr_cli poll attempts in stabilize/apply-fabric (×~2s each)
# LAB_SR_CLI_TRIES_SPINE=90   fabric stagger spine wait (make up)
# LAB_SR_CLI_TRIES_LEAF=120   fabric stagger leaf wait (make up)
# LAB_SR_CLI_TRIES_ALL=90     final all-node sr_cli pass (make up)
#
# WSL / resource-constrained Windows laptops (slower, more reliable):
# LAB_STAGGER_SECS=45

# Audit logging (local/state/lab-actions.log, docker-events.log). make lab-log-status
# LAB_LOG_DISABLE=1         turn off script/make audit log
# LAB_LOG_EVENTS=0          do not auto-start docker events capture on make up/stabilize
# LAB_STABILIZE_WAIT_SECS=60
# LAB_SR_CLI_TRIES=150
# LAB_SR_CLI_TRIES_LEAF=150

# WSL /mnt/c: fabric deploy mirrors to native ext4 (startup-config + clab labdir).
# Default: ~/.cache/network-o11y-demo/clab — override if you prefer another path.
# CLAB_EXT4_ROOT=/home/you/projects/network-o11y-demo/local
# CLAB_FORCE_EXT4=1
